  {
   "evidence_id": "pr:pypa/pipx#2009:comment:0",
   "payload": {
    "author": "SirHegel",
    "author_is_bot": false,
    "body": "Closing \u2014 #2007 predates this by five days and fixes #2005 more surgically: it threads an explicit `prog` through `get_command_parser()` so only `build_parser()` overrides it, leaving `prog_name()` alone.\n\nOne difference worth having on record, since the two are not equivalent in scope. #2007 fixes the docs build. This one changed `prog_name()` itself to fall back to `\"pipx\"` whenever `argv[0]` is neither a `pipx*` binary nor `__main__.py`, which also covers any *other* host process that imports the parser \u2014 a test runner, an embedding tool. Whether that wider behaviour is wanted is a design call, not a bug fix, so #2007 is the right shape for this issue.\n\nSorry for the duplicate; I filtered #2005 on having no assignee and no comments and did not check for a PR already referencing it."
   },
   "source": "github",
   "timestamp": "2026-08-20T19:40:09+00:00",
